# SemText npl-vos — psychodynamic bracket, all display states
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house convention). Three example panels in one
# frame, one per display state the tag provides: the enhanced phase'd bracket
# (entry chip + five labelled rows), the enhanced phase-less bracket (rows
# only, no chip, never an empty mark), and the JS-off degraded form (part
# names as quiet lead-ins over plain authored prose). The exit phase shares
# the phase'd panel's anatomy — only the chip's word/tint changes — so it is
# documented, not paneled (an abstract mock cannot show a word difference).
# The invariant the design must broadcast: npl-vos is display-only and ASIDE-
# flavored — a quiet bracket alongside the persona's response. It never
# occludes, blurs, or hides the authored text (occlusion belongs to the
# sem-spoiler / quiz tier), and the phase-less state never mints an empty
# chip.
#
# MODE 1 — enhanced, phase'd (phase="entry"; exit identical + different word):
#   visible: a small fully-rounded pill chip at the panel's top-left — a
#     hairline accent border, a barely-there accent tint fill, small-caps
#     placeholder bar inside (bright, near-white); below it five stacked
#     rows, each led by a short muted accent-tinted small-caps label bar
#     (right-aligned against a consistent left label column) followed by a
#     wider near-white value bar; a thin accent rule runs down the left of
#     the row group.
#   must never: fill the chip opaque; blur or dim any value bar below its
#     label; place the chip after the rows; let label bars outweigh values.
# MODE 2 — enhanced, phase-less (no phase attribute):
#   visible: the identical five-row anatomy minus the chip — no pill, no
#     empty mark where the chip would sit; the rows start at the panel top.
#   must never: show a pill, a chip-shaped gap, or any empty placeholder
#     mark; restyle rows differently from mode 1.
# MODE 3 — JS-off degraded:
#   visible: each authored line as plain foreground prose led by a short
#     muted small-caps lead-in bar (the part name) — no pill, no rows, no
#     accent rule, no generated chrome; reads as unstyled authored text with
#     quiet captions.
#   must never: show a pill, a row grid, a border rule, or any accent tint;
#     hide or restyle any authored line.
#
# Reference renders: the site's /reference/npl-vos/ page is source-view only
# today (the npl namespace ships upstream, not into the site bundle), so the
# enhanced form is judged from a throwaway fixture captured with headless
# Chrome (canonical example from web/data/elements.json + themes/_vocabulary.css
# + the privately built npl.js). `npl-vos-render-enhanced-900.png` is that
# fixture (entry / exit / phase-less blocks); `npl-vos-render-jsoff-900.png`
# is the same fixture without the script; `npl-vos-fullpage-1280.png` is the
# site page (source view + page chrome) from `npm run snap:tag -- npl-vos`.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-vos
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of three side-by-side reference-page panels
    illustrating one psychodynamic-state bracket element in its three
    display states, wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-
    like, not 3D). Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely
    visible thin grid and a faint violet radial glow upper-left. Three
    equal panels sit side by side, separated by thin slate hairline
    dividers, each panel a dark slate card (#1E293B) with a thin slate
    hairline border, squared corners, deep soft shadow; a small dim
    caption bar sits above each panel.

    LEFT panel — ENHANCED PHASE'D. At the panel's top-left sits a small
    fully-rounded pill chip: hairline violet border, a barely-there violet
    tint fill (never solid), and one short small-caps placeholder bar
    inside it in bright near-white. Below the chip, a row group with a
    thin violet accent rule running down its left edge: five stacked rows,
    each row led by a short, muted, violet-tinted small-caps label bar
    (all labels right-aligned against one shared label column) followed by
    a wider brighter near-white value bar of differing length; the labels
    stay clearly dimmer than their values.

    MIDDLE panel — ENHANCED PHASE-LESS. The identical row group — same
    five rows, same right-aligned label bars, same thin violet left rule —
    starting at the panel's top-left with NO pill chip above it, no chip-
    shaped gap, no empty placeholder mark. Pixel-comparable row anatomy to
    the left panel below the chip line.

    RIGHT panel — JS-OFF DEGRADED. No pill, no rows, no rule, no tint: two
    or three plain prose lines of near-white placeholder bars, each line
    led by a short, muted, dimmer small-caps lead-in bar (the part name)
    sitting inline before it. It must read as unstyled authored prose with
    quiet captions — no grid, no border, no generated chrome.

    Across all three panels the bracket stays quiet and aside-flavored; no
    line of text is occluded, blurred, or dimmed below its label; the
    value bars always outweigh the label bars.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, 3D, photorealism,
    faces, avatars, robot mascots, more than three panels, an opaque filled
    chip, a solid colour-block pill, a pill or empty chip-shaped gap in the
    middle panel, any pill/grid/rule in the right panel, a value bar dimmer
    than its label, an occluded or blurred line
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, three-panel state comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-vos/npl-vos-render-enhanced-900.png
    role: reference
    description: enhanced render — entry chip + five labelled rows, exit chip + four rows, phase-less rows only (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-vos/npl-vos-render-jsoff-900.png
    role: reference
    description: JS-off render — part names as muted small-caps lead-ins over plain prose (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-vos/npl-vos-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: site reference page (source view) — page chrome, attribute table, example and variant placement

requirements:
  subject: three panels of one psychodynamic-state bracket — left enhanced
    phase'd bracket (pill chip + five labelled rows with a thin accent left
    rule), middle enhanced phase-less bracket (same rows, no chip), right
    JS-off plain prose with muted small-caps lead-ins
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet
    accent on the chip tint and left rule, near-white value bars, muted
    violet-tinted labels
  composition: three equal panels side by side; the row group starts at a
    consistent top-left position in every panel; identical row anatomy
    across the two enhanced panels; labels right-aligned to one shared
    label column
  do:
    - keep the chip a small tinted pill with a hairline border, never opaque
    - keep every value bar brighter than its small-caps label
    - differentiate states only by chip presence (left) and chrome presence
      (right)
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, real emoji, or logos
    - an empty chip or chip-shaped gap in the phase-less panel
    - occluding, blurring, or dimming any line in any panel
    - a pill, row grid, or accent rule in the JS-off panel
    - extra chrome (counts, buttons, icons) the tag does not define

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - state_differentiation
    - quiet_not_opaque
  criteria:
    state_differentiation:
      weight: 3
      description: Left panel shows the pill chip plus a five-row labelled
        group; middle shows the identical row group with no chip and no
        empty mark; right shows plain prose lines with small muted lead-in
        bars and no generated chrome
      fail_signals:
        - pill or empty chip-shaped gap present in the middle panel
        - row grid or accent rule present in the right panel
        - chip missing from the left panel
        - row anatomy differs between the two enhanced panels
    quiet_not_opaque:
      weight: 3
      description: The chip is a small tinted pill with a hairline border,
        never a solid opaque block, and no text is occluded, blurred, or
        dimmed below its label in any panel
      fail_signals:
        - opaque or solid accent-filled chip
        - value bars dimmer than their labels
        - blur, redaction, or occlusion overlays on any bar
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style
      fail_signals:
        - light theme
        - glossy 3D look
        - rounded card corners
  reject_if:
    - any legible text, letters, digits, real emoji, watermark, or logo
    - an occluded, blurred, or hidden line in any panel
    - an empty chip or chip-shaped gap in the phase-less panel
    - a pill, grid, or accent rule in the JS-off panel
    - more than three panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-vos
